; A selector parameter: a reusable step acts on the part it is given (SPEC.md §6)
storey[part](h) = x[new&inner](h) i[part](0.3)
storey[top](1.2) x[+z] C                      ; on the lid: inset it, then raise what the inset made
storey(1.2) x[+z] C                           ; no selector: all
storey[+x](0.5) C                             ; on the cube's +x face
storey[part&top](1) x[+z] C                   ; a name used as a selector picks that label: none here, so nothing
roof[p] = k[p](0.8)
tower[lot] = roof[lot&top] storey[lot&top](1)^2 x[lot](1){tower}
tower[+z] C                                   ; names with selector parameters inside names
floor[p] = storey[p|-z](0.5)
floor[top] x[+z|-z] C                         ; a passed selector combined with another
labelled[roof] = x[roof](0.5) x[+z]{roof} C   ; the parameter hides the label of the same name
labelled[+x]
twice[s](h) = x[s](h) x[s](h)
twice[top](0.4) x[+z] C                       ; evaluated at each step: the second x picks the first one's lid
